{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:11:02.147Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Your summary is right. The key detail is that the code sorts by **adjusted** p-value before removing duplicate symbols, so when several probes map to one gene, it keeps the probe with the smallest adjusted p-value.\n\nIn this example, the row counts go from 10 results, to 8 with a usable annotation, to 6 passing the adjusted-p-value cutoff, to 5 distinct genes. `table(best$direction)` shows three down and two up. The direction labels are relative to the contrast used to calculate `logFC`.\n\nI expanded the explanation in the notebook to connect each step to these results and saved it. The existing notebook preview is updated.\n\n[Open the updated notebook](/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb)","date":"2026-11-25T14:12:00.467Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:c55e0c23-5530-4d2d-babd-7dc428ebcf8a","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.c55e0c23-5530-4d2d-babd-7dc428ebcf8a","acp_started_at_ms":1795615885278,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"c55e0c23-5530-4d2d-babd-7dc428ebcf8a","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"3b87df6b-399e-4fe9-b557-6b8ff543e1d4","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":48674,"cached_input_tokens":47202,"output_tokens":276,"reasoning_output_tokens":108,"total_tokens":48950,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:20:08.541Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"```r\n# Rename the annotation table's first column so it matches the probe ID\n# column in results. The values stay the same; only the column name changes.\ncolnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\n\n# Join each result to its gene annotation. all.x = TRUE keeps every row\n# from results, even if a probe has no matching annotation.\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\n\n# Keep rows with a usable gene symbol: neither missing (NA) nor blank (\"\").\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\n\n# Keep probe results whose adjusted p-value is below 0.05.\n# The adjusted value accounts for testing many probes.\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\n\n# Label positive log fold changes \"up\" and zero or negative values \"down\".\n# The direction is relative to the contrast used to calculate logFC.\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\n\n# Sort from smallest to largest adjusted p-value, so the strongest\n# statistical evidence for each gene comes first.\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\n\n# Keep only the first row for each gene symbol. Because sig is sorted,\n# this keeps the probe with the smallest adjusted p-value for each gene.\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\n\n# Reset row names to consecutive numbers after filtering.\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n\n# Print the number of probe rows at each stage: merged, annotated,\n# significant, and reduced to one probe per gene.\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\n\n# Display the selected probe result for each gene.\nbest\n\n# Count how many selected genes are labeled \"up\" and \"down\".\ntable(best$direction)\n```","date":"2026-11-25T14:20:16.484Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:467ca38d-4f61-46fb-a6d0-f720d9cd2875","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.467ca38d-4f61-46fb-a6d0-f720d9cd2875","acp_started_at_ms":1795616409079,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"467ca38d-4f61-46fb-a6d0-f720d9cd2875","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"195c8e42-50bd-4f57-9552-3e3beef575ed","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":51768,"cached_input_tokens":48671,"output_tokens":782,"reasoning_output_tokens":379,"total_tokens":52550,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:24:40.896Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"```r\nlibrary(tidyverse)\n\n# Join each result to its gene annotation. Rename the annotation key inside\n# the pipe so the original annot table stays unchanged.\nmerged_tidy <- results %>%\n  left_join(\n    annot %>% rename(probe = probe_id),\n    by = \"probe\"\n  )\n\n# Keep rows with a nonmissing, nonblank gene symbol.\nannotated_tidy <- merged_tidy %>%\n  filter(!is.na(symbol), symbol != \"\")\n\n# Keep results below the adjusted p-value cutoff and label their direction.\nsig_tidy <- annotated_tidy %>%\n  filter(adj.P.Val < 0.05) %>%\n  mutate(direction = if_else(logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")) %>%\n  # Put the smallest adjusted p-values first before selecting one row per gene.\n  arrange(adj.P.Val)\n\n# Keep the first probe set for each gene symbol, which is now the one with the\n# smallest adjusted p-value.\nbest_tidy <- sig_tidy %>%\n  distinct(symbol, .keep_all = TRUE)\n\n# Show the number of rows at each stage.\nbind_rows(\n  merged_tidy    %>% summarise(stage = \"merged\",    rows = n()),\n  annotated_tidy %>% summarise(stage = \"annotated\", rows = n()),\n  sig_tidy       %>% summarise(stage = \"sig\",       rows = n()),\n  best_tidy      %>% summarise(stage = \"best_tidy\", rows = n())\n)\n\n# Display the selected probe set for each gene.\nbest_tidy\n\n# Count the selected genes in each direction.\ncount(best_tidy, direction)\n```\n\nBecause `best_tidy` is a tibble, resetting row names isn’t needed.","date":"2026-11-25T14:24:57.992Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:a927c7d8-d322-434f-9e8d-5fbd00da4177","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.a927c7d8-d322-434f-9e8d-5fbd00da4177","acp_started_at_ms":1795616681947,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"a927c7d8-d322-434f-9e8d-5fbd00da4177","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"15822310-92ba-4555-a484-869e774bad66","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":55397,"cached_input_tokens":51765,"output_tokens":2060,"reasoning_output_tokens":1688,"total_tokens":57457,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:27:33.851Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"The earlier base R code renamed `annot`’s first column **in place** to `probe`. So if you ran it first, `probe_id` no longer exists and `rename(probe = probe_id)` errors.\n\nThis version handles either column name: it renames `probe_id` when present, and leaves `probe` as is.\n\n```r\nlibrary(tidyverse)\n\nmerged_tidy <- results %>%\n  left_join(\n    annot %>%\n      rename_with(~ \"probe\", .cols = any_of(\"probe_id\")),\n    by = \"probe\"\n  )\n\nannotated_tidy <- merged_tidy %>%\n  filter(!is.na(symbol), symbol != \"\")\n\nsig_tidy <- annotated_tidy %>%\n  filter(adj.P.Val < 0.05) %>%\n  mutate(direction = if_else(logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")) %>%\n  arrange(adj.P.Val)\n\nbest_tidy <- sig_tidy %>%\n  distinct(symbol, .keep_all = TRUE)\n\nbind_rows(\n  merged_tidy    %>% summarise(stage = \"merged\",    rows = n()),\n  annotated_tidy %>% summarise(stage = \"annotated\", rows = n()),\n  sig_tidy       %>% summarise(stage = \"sig\",       rows = n()),\n  best_tidy      %>% summarise(stage = \"best_tidy\", rows = n())\n)\n\nbest_tidy\ncount(best_tidy, direction)\n```","date":"2026-11-25T14:27:50.315Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:1d35b366-ddf1-4361-8e4b-13deea2c5758","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.1d35b366-ddf1-4361-8e4b-13deea2c5758","acp_started_at_ms":1795616855170,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"1d35b366-ddf1-4361-8e4b-13deea2c5758","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"a73da669-d72a-4001-a331-545f80612e7a","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":60279,"cached_input_tokens":55394,"output_tokens":1766,"reasoning_output_tokens":1455,"total_tokens":62045,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:33:26.766Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Two alternatives are:\n\n1. **Choose the probe with the highest average expression** across samples. It may be easier to measure reliably, though high expression doesn’t guarantee the probe is more specific to the gene.\n2. **Choose the probe with the highest variance** across samples. It captures the probe that varies most, but that variation could also reflect noise or outliers.\n\nWhichever rule you use, state it in advance: the choice can change a gene’s reported fold change and direction.","date":"2026-11-25T14:33:33.864Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:beca6e75-dc52-49af-bcc0-02a4019ffb58","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.beca6e75-dc52-49af-bcc0-02a4019ffb58","acp_started_at_ms":1795617207558,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"beca6e75-dc52-49af-bcc0-02a4019ffb58","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"8873d86c-5fbf-4d27-a863-ab285f5bf02c","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":64867,"cached_input_tokens":60276,"output_tokens":550,"reasoning_output_tokens":445,"total_tokens":65417,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T14:34:40.389Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"If several probes map to the same gene, the one with the highest variance has the most changing expression values across the samples. Someone might choose it as the probe that captures the strongest signal, rather than a probe whose values barely change.\n\nBut high variance can also come from noise or an outlier. So this rule doesn’t prove the probe is better; it’s a selection choice that should be stated and applied consistently.","date":"2026-11-25T14:34:45.912Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:20ba2e47-f7ab-4559-a456-443cf529d24c","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.20ba2e47-f7ab-4559-a456-443cf529d24c","acp_started_at_ms":1795617281624,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"20ba2e47-f7ab-4559-a456-443cf529d24c","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"9d6670ac-afe6-4b31-8087-0e7557f28758","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":68222,"cached_input_tokens":64864,"output_tokens":379,"reasoning_output_tokens":289,"total_tokens":68601,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6.1-sol","date":"2026-11-25T14:08:10.637Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6.1-sol","content":"I added a Markdown explanation immediately after the selected code in the live notebook and saved it. The code itself is unchanged.\n\nIt explains how the code:\n\n- Renames the annotation key and joins annotations to the results, keeping result rows even when an annotation is missing.\n- Removes missing or blank gene symbols, then filters for adjusted p-values below 0.05.\n- Labels each result by the sign of its log fold change; “up” and “down” depend on how the contrast was defined.\n- Sorts by adjusted p-value and keeps the first probe set for each gene—the one with the smallest adjusted p-value.\n- Resets row names, reports row counts, displays the selected rows, and counts their directions.\n\nFor the example tables, the row counts are 10, 8, 6, and 5. I verified the explanation’s position in the live notebook and published the updated notebook as a file preview.\n\n[Open the updated notebook](/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb)","date":"2026-11-25T14:11:23.553Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21.chat","acp_log_key":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e:0303f7c1-bec4-46ff-9a22-162641ea0c16","acp_log_subject":"project.f0631fbb-a9b9-4a5a-a705-f650e77c53ab.acp-log.e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e.0303f7c1-bec4-46ff-9a22-162641ea0c16","acp_started_at_ms":1795615691507,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"db8b3017-111f-470e-83b7-1e18effc4a21","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"0303f7c1-bec4-46ff-9a22-162641ea0c16","thread_id":"e595ebb2-835c-4a11-b811-d974e1b2782e","parent_message_id":"efec4131-f3af-4370-ad7b-98805cb4271f","acp_thread_id":"01a21309-2846-7023-9287-27ea6439c907","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":32024,"cached_input_tokens":30607,"output_tokens":557,"reasoning_output_tokens":336,"total_tokens":32581,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
